<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  Cyclone DDS, loopback only, no multicast.

  Why not the default Fast DDS: its shared-memory transport cannot work on
  this machine. Every node logs

      RTPS_TRANSPORT_SHM Error: Failed init_port fastrtps_port7002:
      open_and_lock_file failed

  because the lock files under /tmp/boost_interprocess go stale whenever a ROS
  process is killed rather than shut down cleanly, and a stale lock is never
  reclaimed. Fast DDS does not treat that as fatal - it keeps the participant
  alive and quietly drops the traffic that should have gone over shared
  memory. On the cat that surfaces as gait_controller logging

      no /cmd_vel for 1.7s - holding stance

  in the middle of a walk: the cat stutters, veers tens of degrees off course
  and looks lame, while the head and tail keep working perfectly. That
  asymmetry is the tell - they are plain position setpoints and do not care
  about a dropped message, whereas the gait has a 0.5 s watchdog that stops
  the legs outright.

  Forcing Fast DDS onto UDP alone does not help either: the VPN on this
  machine claims the whole 224.0.0.0/4 multicast range (the same reason
  GZ_IP is pinned to loopback), so its discovery cannot get through.

  Cyclone keeps no lock files at all, and its localhost setup is one block:
  bind to loopback, no multicast, and find peers by unicast on localhost.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <General>
      <Interfaces>
        <NetworkInterface address="127.0.0.1"/>
      </Interfaces>
      <AllowMulticast>false</AllowMulticast>
      <EnableMulticastLoopback>false</EnableMulticastLoopback>
    </General>
    <Discovery>
      <ParticipantIndex>auto</ParticipantIndex>
      <!-- One simulation puts a lot of participants on the host: the Gazebo
           server with the controller manager and four controllers, the state
           publisher, the gait node, the teleop, plus any ros2 CLI call. The
           default ceiling of 9 is not enough headroom. -->
      <MaxAutoParticipantIndex>60</MaxAutoParticipantIndex>
      <Peers>
        <Peer address="localhost"/>
      </Peers>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
